          "id": "8d36bbaf9954c0535be8008ab43028a8c1144588",
          "message": "fix(bench): noise floor for µs-scale timing metrics in the hard zone — measured honest bands exceed 2x (#3753)\n\n* fix(bench): noise floor for µs-scale timing metrics in the hard zone\n\nMeasured 2026-07-23 replay against the published benchmark-data history\nshows honest run-to-run noise bands on µs-scale timing metrics EXCEEDING\nthe 2.0x hard threshold (bands documented at the NOISE_FLOOR constant),\nso the median-of-history gate reds on noise even with clean history —\nthe honest published head replays to a hard fail under the old gate\n(vectors_hnsw_recall_at10 3.00x on its honest 1<->4 oscillation).\n\n* NOISE_FLOOR = 20.0: a NOISY-classified metric whose median-of-window\n  is under the floor can never hard-fail the gate alone — it stays in\n  the watch table flagged \"under noise floor — watch only\" and emits a\n  ::warning at >= 2.0x. Deterministic metrics are NEVER floor-exempt.\n* Reclassify unit \"milli\" as noisy: vectors_hnsw_recall_at10 honestly\n  oscillates 1<->4 (randomized HNSW build, degenerate integer-milli\n  resolution) — a measurement, not a deterministic output; its stable\n  siblings (diskann/pq) sit above the floor and stay hard-gated.\n* Uniform-shift exemption now computes breadth/uniformity/cap over the\n  GATED (non-floor-exempt) rows only — degenerate sub-floor ratios\n  would distort all three.\n* --self-test: sub-floor 3x watch-only vs above-floor 3x hard-fail\n  (mutation-checked: NOISE_FLOOR->0 flips exactly the floor checks\n  red), sub-floor deterministic 2x still fails, exemption-exclusion\n  cases; existing hard-zone fixtures scaled above the floor (43 checks).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(bench): unit-aware noise floor + durable trail for floor-exempt hard-band hits\n\nRound-2 review fixes on the hard-zone noise floor (PR #3753):\n\n* [P1] UNIT-AWARE floor: the raw `median < 20` floor was unit-blind — it\n  wrongly exempted the nine `s`-unit series (load_s/text_build_s/rdfs_infer_s\n  at ~0.4-15 s), parse_ns_per_byte and a ratio metric, so a stable 10x load_s\n  regression would pass and rebase the median. Replaced with an explicit\n  FLOOR_EXEMPT_UNITS allow-list of (unit, floor) pairs — \"us\" < 20.0 and\n  \"milli\" < 20.0 (the empirically-degenerate HNSW recall family), each floor\n  justified by measured honest bands. Every other unit (s, ns_per_byte,\n  ratio, *_per_s, unknown) is NEVER floor-exempt: unknown units fail toward\n  gated. New self-tests: s-unit median 0.4 at 10x hard-fails (mutation-\n  checked: adding \"s\" to the allow-list turns exactly that check red);\n  ns_per_byte/ratio/unknown/absent units stay gated; milli stays exempt.\n\n* [P1] DURABLE TRAIL: floor-exempt hits at >= 2.0x median never red the gate\n  and the median rebases after ~3 accepted points, so a persistent sub-floor\n  regression left no record (emit_report warned once; triage --mode soft\n  files only part[\"soft\"] and its own hard partition is ignored). The gate\n  now writes those rows (--report-out bench-hardzone-report.json) in the\n  triage comparison shape (previous = median-of-history, tagged\n  \"floor-exempt hard-band\"), and bench-triage.py --hardzone-report merges\n  them into the SOFT partition — every hit lands in the rolling deduped\n  bench-flake issue. Triage extension was necessary: it rebuilds its own\n  single-previous-point comparison and never read the hardzone output.\n  Fail-soft (absent/corrupt report = no-op), never weakens a gate.\n\n* [P2] The uniform-shift ::warning now reports the GATED numerator/\n  denominator (\"N of M GATED metrics\", \"no GATED metric reached 4x\") instead\n  of total-row numbers — the predicate is computed over gated rows only, and\n  the old \"no metric reached 4x\" wording was false whenever a floor-exempt\n  row honestly spiked past the cap. Self-test captures the annotation.\n\nBoth --self-test suites green (hardzone 54 checks); test_ci_select_wiring.py\ngreen (66 tests — step names/guards unchanged, so no pin updates).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(bench): round-3 review — fail-soft report typing, Markdown-escaped issue fields, gated-only exemption prose\n\nFour round-3 review findings on the hardzone noise-floor branch:\n\n1. bench-triage.py --hardzone-report loader: {\"floor_exempt_hard\": null} /\n   a number / a non-object top level now degrade to zero merged rows with\n   a warning instead of TypeError-aborting ordinary soft filing; malformed\n   rows dropped with a counted warning.\n2. bench-triage.py issue bodies: artifact-derived metric names/units/notes\n   (and the regression body's rows + suspect subjects) are sanitized before\n   Markdown interpolation — newlines stripped, pipes/backticks escaped\n   (code-span cells defuse backticks and use GFM's \\| escape), @-mentions\n   split with an empty HTML comment.\n3. bench_hardzone.py render_report: stdout + step-summary exemption prose\n   now claims \"no GATED metric reached 4x\" (floor-exempt excluded) — the\n   unqualified \"no >= 4x outlier\" was false when a floor-exempt row sat\n   at/above the cap; annotation self-test extended to cover both sinks.\n4. bench-triage.py flake-issue preamble: when floor-exempt hard-band rows\n   are merged, the body distinguishes soft-band rows from floor-exempt\n   hard-band rows instead of claiming everything is below the hard\n   threshold.\n\nSelf-tests extended for 1 (null/number/non-object payloads) and 2\n(pipe/backtick/newline/@ metric renders escaped); finding 2's new test\nmutation-checked (escape-off flip goes red, restore green).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(bench): round-4 review — guarded numeric admission, defense-in-depth HTML+Markdown sanitizer, class-accurate preamble\n\n1. Numeric admission (_finite_num): every numeric field consumed from an\n   artifact (hardzone-report rows, comparison rows, results values, data.js\n   values/dates) admits only real finite numbers — bool rejected, NaN/Infinity\n   rejected, and the float() conversion itself guarded (10**400 raises\n   OverflowError: dropped with a counted warning, never a crash). Same guard in\n   bench_hardzone._is_num, which previously crashed on out-of-float-range ints.\n2. Injection sinks: one defense-in-depth _sanitize routes EVERY interpolated\n   string in issue bodies — html-escape (&, <, >) first, killing raw-HTML\n   breakouts like </td></table><h1> (GitHub renders raw HTML in bodies), then\n   the existing Markdown layer (newline-strip, pipe/backslash/backtick per cell\n   type, @-defusal). All flake/regression body sinks audited and routed: suite,\n   run_url, SHAs, units, notes, commit subjects, overlap crates; link\n   destinations percent-encoded via _md_url. Self-tested: a forged\n   </td></tr></table><h1>forged</h1> renders fully &lt;-escaped; mutation-checked\n   (disabling the html-escape step reds the forged-table test).\n3. Preamble class sentence derived from the row classes ACTUALLY present —\n   soft-only / floor-exempt-only / mixed three-way; the floor-exempt-only case\n   is self-tested to claim neither 'two classes' nor the soft-zone framing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
