          "distinct": true,
          "id": "d16c420da199564759c0a49c1eb5b303d7caec5d",
          "message": "fix(ci): a stale-ref import and a whole-repo sweep must not brick the gating arm check (#3775)\n\n* fix(ci): a missing transient-retry helper must not brick the gating arm check on every stale branch\n\n`arm reviewed PRs` is a GATING check and auto-arm.yml runs on `pull_request`, so\nGitHub resolves the WORKFLOW FILE (and therefore its file-by-file `sparse-checkout`\nmanifest) from the PR's own ref, while that workflow's checkout step resolves the\nSCRIPT from `ref: default_branch`. #3766 (6137b7b3, 2026-07-25T01:38:35Z) added\n`import gh_retry` to scripts/auto-arm.py AND `scripts/gh_retry.py` to the manifest in\none commit — atomic on main, not atomic across refs. Every PR ref whose workflow\nsnapshot predates 01:38Z still enumerates `scripts/auto-arm.py` alone, so the runner\npaired the NEW default-branch script with a checkout that never materialised\ngh_retry.py:\n\n    File \"/home/runner/work/sparq/sparq/scripts/auto-arm.py\", line 46, in <module>\n      import gh_retry\n  ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'gh_retry'\n\n(#3434, run 30143852994.) ci-summary fail-fasts on a failing gating check, so no\nreviewed PR on a stale ref could merge — a missing RESILIENCE helper became a merge\nblocker.\n\nSURVIVABILITY (heals the already-stale refs). Guard the import in both arm scripts.\nThe stale refs cannot be rewritten, so their manifest is frozen and no workflow edit\ncan reach them; only default-branch CODE does. On ImportError each script emits ONE\nloud ::warning naming cause and remedy and proceeds with one-shot `gh` reads. The\ndegradation is deliberate and documented: reads lose their retries, a read failure is\nGhFatalError (never the lenient GhTransientExhausted, which #3759 converts to\n::warning + exit 0), assert_read_only stays a real fail-closed guard rather than a\nno-op, and the arm decision plus both mutations still happen.\n\nIMPOSSIBILITY (stops new skew). Both arm workflows now sparse-check out the whole\n`scripts` directory in cone mode instead of enumerating files, so a future sibling\nimport cannot be missed.\n\nTests (scripts/tests/test_arm_capability_wiring.py, run by docs-quality):\neach script's self-test must pass from a directory holding only that file; the\ndegraded path must still issue `gh pr ready` and the arm mutation; the degraded\nread-only guard must still refuse mutations; the real helper must be used when\nimportable; no workflow may enumerate a .py file whose sibling imports it omits; and\nno scripts/*.py may shadow a stdlib module (a hazard the whole-directory checkout\nintroduces).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ci): an event-triggered auto-arm run judges only the PR that triggered it\n\n`AutoArmer.run()` swept EVERY open `review:pass` PR in BOTH modes. #3766 then made\nthe exit status sticky over collected failures — correct for the cron sweep, but\ncombined with whole-repo scope on a GATING check it meant ONE permanently\nun-armable PR redded `arm reviewed PRs` on every OTHER PR's label event.\n\nMeasured blast radius (run 30144214363, 2026-07-25T04:33Z): sparq had exactly two\n`review:pass` PRs and the run reported `considered=2 armed=0 arm-failures=1` —\n#3434 cannot be armed at all until the `workflows: write` question (#3777) is\ndecided, so the gating arm check was poisoned repository-wide by one PR.\n\nIn `--mode event` the run is now scoped to the triggering PR. Scope (WHICH PRs a\nrun is accountable for) and mode (how loud a missed cycle is, #3759 finding 5)\nare separate axes. `--mode sweep` keeps whole-repo scope and its lenient\ntransient policy, so the cron remains the backstop.\n\nThis NARROWS accountability, it does not weaken it: within its own scope #3766's\nprecedence is untouched — the triggering PR's own arm failure is still a hard\nnon-zero exit that no later transient can discard.\n\nThe number reaches the script two ways, deliberately. auto-arm.yml passes\n`--pr ${{ github.event.pull_request.number }}` (forward-looking), and the script\nalso derives it from the runner environment (GITHUB_EVENT_PATH / GITHUB_REF) —\nthe workflow file is snapshotted per PR ref, which is the #3776 skew itself, so\nonly the default-branch script can scope an already-frozen ref.\n\nDe-gating `arm reviewed PRs` is deliberately NOT done here: that is a policy\ndecision about what may block a merge, not a correctness fix. See #3777.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-25T06:32:23+01:00",
